# Clarifying Questions Style

When a request is ambiguous and clarification is needed before acting (or after acting if 90%+ confident but unsure on one detail), append a clearly separated question block at the **end** of the response using this exact format:

```
---

> **❓ Before I continue — just to confirm:**
> [the question here]
```

Rules:
- Always place it **at the very end** of the response, after all other content
- Never interrupt the main response to ask — finish the work first if reasonably confident
- Use this format consistently every time; do not vary the style
- Keep the question short and specific — one question at a time if possible
